// S~S  SimpleSal signal starts  S~S

Consider the STEAM projects in terms of increasing complexity

blink:  BUILTIN_LED manipulation using DELAY (proves build capability)

timed blink: blink with build- or run-time control of the rate of blinking

triggered blink:  blink at a rate when a sensor value triggers the blink

with added sensor, adapt “blink” into “unlock or lock”

with added co-device, create local data access and protocols (bit bus)

with added co-device, adapt “blink” into a “push data to host” protocol

with added co-device, adapt “push data to host” into  “push button on wall”

Complexity is reduced by giving up responsibility for features

interacting with two devices over Time at two different rates (LED, sensor)

// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S


